{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Review care pathways for women with suspected endometriosis",
        "additional_details": "Endometriosis can cause severe, life-changing symptoms, yet many women face long waits, repeated appointments and investigations without a clear diagnosis or plan. When investigations are inconclusive, women can be left without support despite continuing to suffer. We want the NHS to provide a clear pathway, including specialist review, further investigation where appropriate and symptom management while women wait. An inconclusive investigation should not mean the end of a woman\u2019s care.",
        "background": "We call on the UK Government to review care pathways for women with persistent symptoms of suspected endometriosis. They should be given a clear pathway to appropriate specialist care, further investigation where clinically appropriate and ongoing symptom management.",
